Note this program was designed to work from the cli/shell and works
perfectly when installed as a dos pfile or as a menu item. It should work
on many bbs programs to include DLG and CNET. Refer to the chess.doc for
information on contacting the author.

Installation:

method one:
	1. Uncrunch the chess program to your pfile directory.

	2. Log onto cnet and enter the pfiles area.

	3. type "ao" to adopt a file

	4. the subdirectory to search will be Pfiles:program

	5. Select "chess" to adopt.

	6. Give the pfile a description of "ANSI CHESS"

	Then select and play the appropriate pfile item number and you and a user
	can play chess.

method two:
	1. place the following line in your cnet:bbsmenu file under the commands
		available everywhere as the last line of this section.

---------------------------------- cut below ----------------------------
	CHESS, ANSI CHESS |#4pfiles:program/chess}
---------------------------------- cut above ----------------------------


